hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3034","Narrated to us ‘Imrān ibn Mūsā al-Qazzāz – on the authority of ‘Abd al-Wārith ibn Sa‘īd – who narrated to us Abū al-Tayyāh – who narrated to us Mūsā ibn Salamah al-Hudhalī who said:

Mu‘tamir (i.e., performing ‘umrah) set out with Sinān ibn Salamah. When we arrived at al-Baṭḥā’, I said, “Let us go to Ibn ‘Abbās so we may speak with him.”
Sinān said to Ibn ‘Abbās, “Indeed, my mother is in the city (al-Miṣr), and I go out on these military expeditions. If I free a slave in her place, will it suffice for her?”
Ibn ‘Abbās replied, “Shall I not tell you of something more amazing than that? I ordered the wife of Sinān ibn ‘Abd Allāh al-Juhanī to ask the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) for me: her mother died and she had not performed ḥajj. Would it suffice for her mother to perform ḥajj on her behalf?”
He (the Prophet ﷺ) said, “Yes. If her mother had a debt, would she have paid it on her behalf? Would it not have sufficed? Then let her perform ḥajj on behalf of her mother.”

---

**CHAPTER:**"
"3035","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn ‘Abdah: narrated to us Hammād ibn Zayd: on the authority of Abū al-Tayyāḥ: on the authority of Mūsā ibn Salamah who said:
I heard Ibn ‘Abbās (RA) say that a man from the Juhaynah tribe said:
“O Messenger of Allāh, my father died while he was an old man who had not performed Hajj, or was unable to perform Hajj.”
He (ﷺ) said:
“Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.”

**CHAPTER:**"
